<article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl py-12 sm:py-16">
  <header>
    <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-700">
      About YouCongress
    </p>
    <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-gray-900 sm:text-5xl">
      Investigate difficult public questions. Together.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-xl leading-8 text-gray-600">
      YouCongress connects concrete proposals with sourced positions, lets people scrutinize the record, and makes agreement and disagreement visible through participation.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-gray-600">
      Our initial focus is AI governance: how societies can manage AI’s risks, shape its effects on jobs and work, and share its benefits. Reducing catastrophic AI risk is an important part of that mission.
    </p>
    <.link
      href={~p"/explore"}
      class="mt-7 inline-flex rounded-lg bg-indigo-600 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white hover:bg-indigo-500"
    >
      Explore proposals <span aria-hidden="true" class="ml-2">→</span>
    </.link>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">Read the sources and arguments without an account.</p>
  </header>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-how" class="py-12">
    <h2 id="about-how" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">What you can do here</h2>
    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 text-left text-gray-700">
      <div class="bg-white/80 border border-indigo-100 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-indigo-600">
          Data layer
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-1">Verifiable sources and claims</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          We track who said what, when, where and in relation to which policy or claim, then invite the community to help keep the record clean.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm">
          <li>
            <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Journalists &amp; policy makers</p>
            <div class="mt-2 rounded-xl border border-indigo-100 bg-indigo-50 px-4 py-3 text-base font-semibold text-indigo-900 shadow-sm">
              Find who said what, with sources.
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Citizens</p>
            <div class="mt-2 rounded-xl border border-amber-100 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-base font-semibold text-amber-900 shadow-sm">
              Want to help on hard public questions but no PhD?
              <p>
                <.link
                  href="mailto:hi@youcongress.org"
                  class="underline text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800"
                >Help</.link>&nbsp;validate the quotes that our AI finds.
              </p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white/80 border border-emerald-100 rounded-2xl p-6 shadow-sm">
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-emerald-700 flex items-center gap-2">
          Participation layer
          <span class="text-[0.6rem] tracking-wide text-white bg-emerald-700 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full">
            beta
          </span>
        </p>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-gray-900 mt-1">Liquid democracy for policy</h3>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-600">
          The source layer connects policies and claims with votes and delegations so collective preferences stay transparent. Sources and verification status remain available to inspect.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm">
          <li>
            <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Politicians &amp; activists</p>
            <p>
              <.link
                href="mailto:hi@youcongress.org"
                class="underline text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800"
              >Propose</.link>&nbsp;a policy proposal or a claim to be analysed and voted.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="font-semibold text-gray-900">Citizens</p>
            <p>
              Add your opinions, vote and delegate to people you trust: users and public figures (we infer their vote from their sourced quotes).
            </p>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-5 text-sm leading-6 text-gray-600">
      Delegation currently applies across issues. Some public figures’ positions are inferred from sourced quotes; that does not mean they personally voted or joined YouCongress.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-why" class="rounded-2xl bg-indigo-50 p-6 sm:p-8">
    <h2 id="about-why" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">Why we’re building this</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-gray-700">
      Evidence is scattered across papers, interviews, speeches, and posts. Understanding a difficult question often means reconstructing the same debate from scratch. We want that work to accumulate into a shared resource that people can inspect, challenge, and improve.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-gray-700">
      Better understanding can help people identify opportunities for cooperation. But visible agreement alone does not change incentives or make institutions act. YouCongress is one contribution to that larger task.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 font-semibold text-indigo-700">
      <.link href={~p"/moloch"} class="underline underline-offset-4">
        Understand coordination failures
      </.link>
      <.link href={~p"/theory-of-change"} class="underline underline-offset-4">
        Read our theory of change
      </.link>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-project" class="py-12">
    <h2 id="about-project" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">An open project</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-gray-600">
      YouCongress is a non-profit project built by <a
        href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/hectorperezarenas"
        class="font-medium text-indigo-700 underline"
      >Hector Perez Arenas</a>. Our
      <a
        href="https://github.com/youcongress/youcongress"
        class="font-medium text-indigo-700 underline"
      >
        code is open source
      </a>
      and our <.link href={~p"/dataset"} class="font-medium text-indigo-700 underline">quote dataset is open</.link>, so others can inspect and reuse the work. AI governance is our first major focus; the approach can also be tested on other public questions.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-gray-600">
      YouCongress received a $5,000 award in the Future of Life Foundation’s Epistemic Case Study Competition. The judges highlighted its participation layer as a promising direction to explore. <.link
        href={~p"/future-of-life-foundation-epistack-award"}
        class="font-medium text-indigo-700 underline"
      >Read about the award and the judges’ remarks</.link>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="about-join" class="border-t border-gray-200 pt-8">
    <h2 id="about-join" class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900">
      Help improve the conversation
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-gray-600">
      Bring a missing source, a well-supported objection, or a question that deserves closer examination.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-5 font-semibold text-indigo-700">
      <.link href={~p"/explore"} class="underline underline-offset-4">Explore proposals</.link>
      <.link :if={!@current_user} href={~p"/sign_up"} class="underline underline-offset-4">
        Join YouCongress
      </.link>
      <.link href={~p"/contact"} class="underline underline-offset-4">Contact us</.link>
      <.link href={~p"/faq"} class="underline underline-offset-4">
        Frequently asked questions
      </.link>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>
